      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Enabling loop on emotes could be a solution to this. Infact, my idle animations are WHY I want loop on emotes.\n\nI threw 8 different idles onto gestures on an avatar... and I had to make 8 duplicates of my model to do it. That avatar takes a lot longer to load than if I could just animate things directly.\n\nNow that disabled gameobjects are counted in performance ranking, I have the stats of having 9 models loaded at once.\n\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/now-that-we-can-cancel-emotes-by-moving-let-us-use-loop-time-on-emotes\n\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/support-gestures-longer-than-2-frames",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-22T23:18:14.198Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As having an extra animation controller on your model has a non-zero performance impact, I would like to request a way to have at least 1 constantly looping animation that runs at all times that is properly integrated into the SDK. Many models use extra anims that run at all times to change values in shape keys and shaders. It would be nice to have an official way of doing this that doesn't require multiple animation controllers, which the performance rating system obviously discourages.",
